title: September 2026

@pis_club_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The former F-grade transition now explains the fifteen-MP rule, names Kaczyński, Morawiecki and the early defectors, distinguishes a club from an association or informal circle, locates Lewica inside each possible cabinet, and gives both responses outcome-specific consequences.
title: Rozwój+ tests whether it can form a Sejm club
subtitle: Fifteen signed departures, not Morawiecki's list of sympathisers, decide the parliamentary institution
face-image: img/poland/events/mateusz-morawiecki-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 27
order: 12
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and ((year = 2026 and month = 9) or (year = 2026 and month = 4 and rozwoj_early_route)) and rozwoj_chain_stage = 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.rozwoj_club_formed = !Q.rozwoj_split_blocked &&
    Q.rozwoj_definitive_departures >= 15 ? 1 : 0;
Q.pis_split = Q.rozwoj_club_formed;
Q.pis_split_crisis = Q.rozwoj_club_formed ? 0 : 1;
if (Q.rozwoj_club_formed) {
    Q.rozwoj_seats =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.rozwoj_seats) || 0) +
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.rozwoj_pending_seats) || 0);
    Q.other_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.other_seats) || 0) -
            (Number(Q.rozwoj_pending_seats) || 0)
    );
    Q.rozwoj_pending_seats = 0;
}
Q.rozwoj_club_seats_2026 = Q.rozwoj_club_formed
    ? Q.rozwoj_seats
    : Q.rozwoj_pending_seats;
Q.pis_morawiecki_camp = Q.rozwoj_club_formed
    ? Q.rozwoj_definitive_departures
    : Q.rozwoj_association_members;
Q.rozwoj_club_result = Q.rozwoj_club_formed
    ? "Rozwój+ parliamentary club formed"
    : "No club; association and informal circle continue";
Q.rozwoj_chain_stage = 4;
const association = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "rozwoj_plus";
});
if (association) {
    association.legal_status = Q.rozwoj_club_formed
        ? "association with parliamentary club"
        : "association with informal parliamentary circle";
    association.exclusive_seats = Q.rozwoj_club_formed
        ? Q.rozwoj_seats
        : Q.rozwoj_pending_seats;
}
Q.news_headline = Q.rozwoj_club_result;
!}

= September 2026 — [+ rozwoj_club_result +]

<span class="party-pis"><b>Mateusz Morawiecki</b></span> brings the signed departure declarations to the Sejm
Chancellery. Former PiS organisers **Olga Semeniuk-Patkowska, Janusz Cieszyński**
and <span class="party-pis"><b>Paweł Jabłoński</b></span> are among the cases resolved one by one; **Jarosław
Kaczyński** has failed to bring them back by party discipline.

[? if rozwoj_club_formed: At least fifteen MPs have now completed their
departures. Their **[+ rozwoj_club_seats_2026 +] seats** form a recognised Rozwój+
parliamentary club with its own leadership, staff and places in Sejm business.
This is a split in PiS's parliamentary camp, not yet a registered political
party.?][? if not rozwoj_club_formed: Fewer than fifteen MPs have completed the
process. **[+ rozwoj_club_seats_2026 +] deputies** remain outside PiS as an
informal circle around the Rozwój+ association, without the fuller rights of a
Sejm club. Morawiecki has a faction and a microphone, not a recognised club or
party.?]

[? if left_in_government and government_party = "pis": Lewica is still inside
the PiS-led cabinet whose working count those departures reduced. Any
non-aggression offer may keep that cabinet alive; any attack is also a choice
to make our own coalition less governable.?][? if left_in_government and
government_party != "pis": Lewica governs elsewhere. Rozwój+ may provide votes
on particular bills, but it has no place in our cabinet without a new formation
agreement.?][? if not left_in_government: From opposition, Lewica can test both
conservative camps vote by vote; it cannot appoint either one as the successor
to PiS.?]

- @pis_club_nonaggression
- @pis_club_attack

@pis_club_nonaggression
title: Offer a vote-by-vote non-aggression protocol
subtitle: Publish the issues on which Lewica will talk, without promising a coalition or forgiving the old cabinet.
on-arrival: coalition_opportunity_pis += 4; pis_relation += 1; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica offers a transparent vote-by-vote protocol"

[? if rozwoj_club_formed: Morawiecki accepts a separate channel for labour law,
hospitals and investment votes. His club gains evidence that it can act without
Kaczyński; Lewica gains leverage and an internal argument over normalising the
architect of the old government.?][? if not rozwoj_club_formed: The informal
circle may sign individual names to the protocol, but it cannot promise a club
line it does not possess. Lewica gains possible votes, not a new parliamentary
partner.?] [? if left_in_government and government_party = "pis": Kaczyński
understands that his coalition partner has opened a survival channel to the MPs
he expelled.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Open the channel

@pis_club_attack
title: Contest the club or circle as developmental conservatism
subtitle: Fight Morawiecki on wages, public services and his governing record instead of treating a personnel split as renewal.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 3; pis_relation -= 2; rozwoj_party_readiness += 3; news_headline = "Lewica contests Rozwój+ on economics rather than personnel"

[? if rozwoj_club_formed: Lewica welcomes the end of Kaczyński's monopoly and
immediately treats the new club as an economic rival. Morawiecki is forced to
turn modernising language into positions on wages, unions and public
investment.?][? if not rozwoj_club_formed: Lewica refuses to inflate an
informal circle into a national alternative and follows each deputy's record
instead. The pressure gives Morawiecki another reason to accelerate party
building.?] [? if left_in_government and government_party = "pis": The attack
also lands inside Lewica's own cabinet, where PiS loyalists demand coalition
discipline.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Contest the ground

@women_boards_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — Kotula, company boards, workers and the EU transposition duty are located in the live cabinet arrangement, while both routes distinguish an externally enacted statute from Lewica's proposal.
title: A boardroom directive reaches Polish politics
subtitle: Kotula asks who governs the companies that govern so much of working life
face-image: img/poland/events/european-parliament.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 20
order: 30
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 9
on-arrival: {!
Q.boards_law_enacted =
    Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government && Q.government_party != "pis" ? 1 : 0;
Q.boards_policy_authority = Q.boards_law_enacted
    ? "Enacted by the Sejm and President; implementation belongs to the responsible economy ministry"
    : (
        Q.caretaker_government
            ? "Caretaker proposal pending the next cabinet"
            : (
                Q.left_in_government
                    ? "Coalition proposal without parliamentary passage"
                    : "Parliamentary opposition proposal"
            )
    );
if (Q.boards_law_enacted) {
    Q.feminist_trust += 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Gender-balance requirements pass for major company leadership";
} else {
    Q.news_headline = Q.caretaker_government
        ? "Caretaker government defers the company-board transposition bill"
        : (
            Q.government_party == "pis"
                ? "The PiS cabinet leaves the company-board transposition bill unenacted"
                : "Lewica remains outside cabinet as the company-board bill stays a proposal"
        );
}
!}

= September 2026 — Representation still needs legal authority

<span class="party-lewica"><b>Katarzyna Kotula</b></span>, Lewica's equality advocate, brings the EU gender-balance
duty into a Polish argument about who occupies the rooms where large companies
set pay, investment and employment policy.

[? if boards_law_enacted: Before this meeting, the Sejm majority behind the
functioning cabinet passed the gender-balance transposition and the President
signed it. The statute is already on the books; today's dispute concerns its
implementation and Lewica's next parliamentary demand. The law redistributes
senior corporate power; it does not by itself change pay or give workers a
seat.?]
[? if not boards_law_enacted and caretaker_government: The caretaker can
prepare the transposition file but cannot bind its successor. Lewica has a
proposal and a deadline, not an enacted rule.?]
[? if not boards_law_enacted and not caretaker_government and left_in_government:
The PiS-led cabinet has left the transposition unenacted. Lewica sits inside
that cabinet and must either force a bill onto its agenda or admit the limit of
its ministries.?]
[? if not boards_law_enacted and not caretaker_government and not
left_in_government: [? if government_party = "pis": The PiS-led cabinet has
left the transposition unenacted.?][? if government_party != "pis": The
governing majority has not completed the transposition, and Lewica holds no
cabinet office from which to administer it.?] From opposition, the party can
table and organise around the missing rule; it cannot order company boards to
obey a bill that has not passed.?]

- @boards_defend
- @boards_expand

@boards_defend
title: [? if boards_law_enacted: Defend representation as a real redistribution of power?][? if not boards_law_enacted: Table the delayed gender-balance transposition bill?]
subtitle: Keep the measure narrow enough to enforce and state plainly whether it is law or a bill.
on-arrival: {!
Q.feminist_trust += 4;
Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
Q.liberal_professionals_left_affinity += 2;
Q.labor_dissent += 1;
if (!Q.boards_law_enacted) {
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Proposal";
    Q.last_policy_authority = Q.boards_policy_authority;
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
}
Q.news_headline = Q.boards_law_enacted
    ? "The Left defends who gets to govern major firms"
    : "Lewica tables the company-board transposition bill from opposition";
!}

[? if boards_law_enacted: The responsible economy ministry publishes the
first covered firms, deadlines and reporting duties. Kotula's team follows the
record and names gaps without pretending to command another portfolio.
Corporate leaders can oppose the rule, but not reduce it to a slogan; women
entering those boards receive a legal claim rather than a request for
goodwill.?][? if not boards_law_enacted: Lewica files the missing
transposition text with reporting duties and enforcement dates. It remains a
proposal under **[+ boards_policy_authority +]**: no company is represented as
bound before Parliament and the competent cabinet act.?] Labour organisers
warn that changing the people at the top does not yet change who answers to the
workforce below.

- @poland_event_queue: File the text

@boards_expand
title: [? if boards_law_enacted: Link board representation to pay transparency and worker seats?][? if not boards_law_enacted: Combine the missing board rules with pay transparency and worker seats?]
subtitle: Join gender balance to pay transparency and elected worker representation, accepting a harder coalition fight.
on-arrival: {!
Q.feminist_trust += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 5;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
if (!Q.boards_law_enacted) {
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Proposal";
    Q.last_policy_authority = Q.boards_policy_authority;
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
}
Q.news_headline = Q.boards_law_enacted
    ? "Representation expands into workplace power"
    : "Lewica publishes a broader workplace-representation bill";
!}

[? if boards_law_enacted: Lewica treats the enacted gender rule as the first
clause of a wider workplace-power bill: published pay gaps and elected worker
seats follow. The existing rule remains law while the expansion returns to
Parliament.?][? if not boards_law_enacted: Kotula and union lawyers publish one
broader bill covering representation, pay information and worker seats. None
of it is yet enacted; combining the demands makes a clearer movement and a
harder parliamentary majority.?] KO's economic liberals accuse Lewica of using
an EU duty to reopen corporate governance itself—which is exactly the choice we
have made.

- @poland_event_queue: File the wider bill

@september_budget_horizon
# prose-audit: Grade A — The Prime Minister, Finance Minister, PSL and Lewica's live cabinet role animate the draft, and every social, rural or fiscal line has a distinct governing or opposition aftermath.
title: The 2027 budget is drafted
subtitle: Defence, health, local services and EU deadlines compete for the same money
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-voting-device.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 24
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 9
on-arrival: {!
Q.horizon_budget_authority =
    Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = Q.horizon_budget_authority
    ? "The pre-election budget begins with incompatible coalition mandates"
    : "Lewica prepares a shadow 2027 budget without claiming treasury authority";
!}

= September 2026 — Five priorities, one limited budget

Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** asks Finance Minister **[+
finance_minister +]** for a draft that can carry defence, health, local
government, EU fiscal pressure and KPO deadlines at once. **Władysław
Kosiniak-Kamysz** arrives with rural services to protect. [? if
ministry_psl_in_cabinet or government_party = "psl": As a cabinet partner, PSL
can bargain over the draft.?][? if not ministry_psl_in_cabinet and
government_party != "psl": From opposition, PSL can offer votes or amendments,
not veto the cabinet's draft.?] Every smaller party is already reading each
concession as a line in its 2027 campaign.

[? if horizon_budget_authority: Lewica shares responsibility for a functioning
cabinet, including a PiS-led one if that is the coalition we built. We do not
own the treasury unless Lewica holds the Finance Ministry, but our ministers
and votes can set a red line that the Prime Minister must fund or break.?]
[? if not horizon_budget_authority and caretaker_government: The caretaker can
keep departments operating, not commit its successor to a political 2027
settlement. Lewica's choices become a costed demand for the next confidence
majority.?]
[? if not horizon_budget_authority and not caretaker_government: Lewica is in
opposition. The choices below produce a shadow budget and amendment line; they
do not spend, save or bind state money.?]

- @horizon_social
- @horizon_rural
- @horizon_fiscal

@horizon_social
title: [? if horizon_budget_authority: Announce health, housing and labour enforcement as non-negotiable?][? if not horizon_budget_authority: Publish a costed shadow package for health, housing and labour enforcement?]
subtitle: Put staffed clinics, homes and labour inspectors ahead of coalition comfort, with costs attached.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget_promises += 4;
Q.party_unity += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.ko_relation -= 4;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
if (Q.horizon_budget_authority) Q.fiscal_stress += 4;
else {
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Proposal";
    Q.last_policy_authority = "Opposition shadow budget";
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
}
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 8;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 6;
Q.news_headline = Q.horizon_budget_authority
    ? "The Left enters the budget round with a funded-delivery ultimatum"
    : "Lewica publishes a costed social shadow budget";
!}

[? if horizon_budget_authority: Lewica's ministers place staffing, housing
construction and labour inspection in the coalition's non-negotiable column.
The Finance Minister must now find revenue or breach the fiscal plan; the
cabinet's fiscal conservatives resent being handed the remaining cuts.[? if
ministry_psl_in_cabinet or government_party = "psl": PSL shares that cabinet
fight.?][? if not ministry_psl_in_cabinet and government_party != "psl": PSL
can criticise the package, but it receives no cabinet cuts to allocate.?] The
party enters winter united around something the cabinet can actually fail to
deliver.?]
[? if not horizon_budget_authority: Lewica publishes departmental costs,
revenues and the amendments that would move money toward clinics, homes and
inspection. No ministry receives a złoty from a shadow document. Government
parties must answer the package rather than dismiss another unpriced demand.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Enter the column

@horizon_rural
title: [? if horizon_budget_authority and (ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl"): Pre-negotiate a rural-social coalition compact with PSL?][? if horizon_budget_authority and ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": Seek opposition PSL votes for a rural-social budget compact?][? if not horizon_budget_authority: Negotiate a joint rural-social amendment platform with PSL?]
subtitle: Trade certainty on rural clinics and local finance for PSL support on housing and labour enforcement.
on-arrival: {!
const pslCabinetLive = Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet || Q.government_party == "psl";
Q.psl_relation += 7;
Q.rural_support += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
if (Q.horizon_budget_authority && pslCabinetLive) {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 2;
}
Q.news_headline = Q.horizon_budget_authority && pslCabinetLive
    ? "PSL receives a reason not to threaten the coalition in December"
    : (
        Q.horizon_budget_authority
            ? "The cabinet seeks opposition PSL votes for a rural-social package"
            : "Lewica and PSL publish a rural-social amendment platform"
    );
!}

[? if horizon_budget_authority and (ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "psl"): Kosiniak-Kamysz accepts a joint cabinet envelope for rural clinics,
bus routes and municipal finance; in return PSL stops treating Lewica's
housing and enforcement funds as the first place to cut. The bargain removes
one December coalition threat and leaves progressives asking which universal
programme paid for geographic peace.?]
[? if horizon_budget_authority and not ministry_psl_in_cabinet and
government_party != "psl": The cabinet offers rural clinics, bus routes and
municipal finance in exchange for PSL votes on housing and labour enforcement.
Kosiniak-Kamysz can support or reject the package from opposition; he cannot
turn that choice into a cabinet ultimatum.?]
[? if not horizon_budget_authority: Lewica and PSL publish matching amendments
for rural services, housing and labour inspection. They cannot bind the
cabinet, but a government that rejects one must now vote against both partners'
district promises in the same division.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Sign with Kosiniak-Kamysz

@horizon_fiscal
title: [? if horizon_budget_authority: Accept a tight ceiling in exchange for protecting enacted programmes?][? if not horizon_budget_authority: Publish a tight-ceiling shadow budget that protects existing programmes?]
subtitle: Protect programmes already in law and surrender the next expansion year to a tighter ceiling.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ko_relation += 5;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 5;
Q.labor_credibility -= 3;
if (Q.horizon_budget_authority) {
    Q.fiscal_stress -= 4;
    Q.budget_breaches += 2;
} else {
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Proposal";
    Q.last_policy_authority = "Opposition shadow budget";
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
    Q.public_trust += 1;
}
Q.news_headline = Q.horizon_budget_authority
    ? "The Left protects its floor and abandons another expansion year"
    : "Lewica publishes a restrained shadow budget without claiming treasury savings";
!}

[? if horizon_budget_authority: Lewica accepts the Finance Minister's ceiling
after securing money for programmes already enacted. The cabinet's arithmetic
improves and KO gains the discipline it demanded. No new social promise fits;
Razem and unions are asked to defend a year in which survival has replaced
advance.?]
[? if not horizon_budget_authority: The shadow budget shows which expansions
Lewica would postpone while protecting existing entitlements. It saves no state
money until adopted, but it denies the government an easy claim that every
opposition promise assumes an unlimited treasury.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Accept the ceiling
